From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tyler Smith <74526874+tylertms@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 21:52:03 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kthread): require native policy reset before publishing
 creation

---
 kernel/kthread.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel/kthread.c b/kernel/kthread.c
index 84d17ab88ef5ccdd892a39cab2e36d1b4ae06cb4..78bc7b20845eb4aad055055aea2354d63b8f6d1e 100644
--- a/kernel/kthread.c
+++ b/kernel/kthread.c
@@ -447,7 +447,11 @@ static int kthread(void *_create)
 	 * The new thread inherited kthreadd's priority and CPU mask. Reset
 	 * back to default in case they have been changed.
 	 */
+#ifdef CONFIG_STELA
+	BUG_ON(sched_setscheduler_nocheck(current, SCHED_NORMAL, &param));
+#else
 	sched_setscheduler_nocheck(current, SCHED_NORMAL, &param);
+#endif
 
 	/* OK, tell user we're spawned, wait for stop or wakeup */
 	__set_current_state(TASK_UNINTERRUPTIBLE);
